Format: https://www.debian.org/doc/packaging-manuals/copyright-format/1.0/
Upstream-Name: marinaMoji
Upstream-Contact: Daniel Patrick Morgan <daniel.morgan@college-de-france.fr>
Source: https://github.com/marinaMoji/marinaMoji
Files-Excluded:
 src/win32
 src/renderer/win32
 src/gui/tool/mozc_tool.rc
 src/server/mozc_server.rc
 src/build_tools/mozc_win32_resource_template.rc
Comment:
 The +ds1 orig tarball drops Windows-only trees and resource scripts that
 the Linux package never builds (same approach as Debian's mozc). See
 packaging/debian/DFSG.md.
 .
 Offline Bazel deps are *not* in the main orig tarball. They ship as a
 second upstream component (orig-vendor.tar.xz → top-level vendor/),
 produced by packaging/debian/offline/vendor_deps.sh on Linux. That keeps
 the DFSG source reviewable separately from the large vendor tree.
 .
 This file is installed verbatim as /usr/share/doc/marinamoji/copyright.
 It therefore also covers material that ends up in the binary package:
 statically linked third-party code (see the vendor/* stanza) and data
 files such as the OpenCC tables, character composer data and icons.
 The third-party apt .deb ships packaging/linux/data/copyright instead,
 which uses install-tree paths; keep the two in sync.

