Files: src/data/character_composer/*
Copyright: CHISE project and contributors
           kawabata (cjkvi-ids)
           2024-2026, Marina Pandolfino and Daniel Patrick Morgan (format conversion)
License: GPL-2+
Comment:
 Character composer data: IDS (ideographic description sequence) tables
 derived from the CHISE IDS project (via github.com/cjkvi/cjkvi-ids and
 github.com/chise/ids). These files are plain data read at run time by
 mozc_tool; they are not compiled or linked into any binary, which stay
 BSD-3-Clause. See src/data/character_composer/README.md.

Files: src/data/character_composer/stroke_counts.tsv
       src/data/character_composer/LICENSE.Unicode
Copyright: 1991-2026, Unicode, Inc.
License: Unicode-3.0
Comment:
 Total stroke counts from the Unicode Unihan database (kTotalStrokes).

Files: src/data/character_info/*
Copyright: 1991-2026, Unicode, Inc. (Unihan data)
           2009, GlyphWiki Project and contributors (itaiji links)
           2014, CJKVI Database (cjkvi-variants.txt pairs)
           2026, marinaMoji contributors (build script)
License: Unicode-3.0 and GlyphWiki-Free-Data and MIT and BSD-3-Clause
Comment:
 char_info.tsv is generated by build_char_info.py from the Unicode Unihan
 database, variant links taken from GlyphWiki glyph names, and the pairs in
 cjkvi-variants.txt (github.com/cjkvi/cjkvi-variants, commit e4f1da2). The
 kanji-database project, which owns that data, declares its 異体字データ
 (variant data) MIT-licensed at https://kanji-database.sourceforge.net/ ; the
 repository itself carries no licence file, only the header "Copyright (c)
 2014 CJKVI Database". The MIT terms are reproduced in the License: MIT
 paragraph below. The notice required by the Unicode licence is in
 UNICODE_NOTICE.txt, which is installed with the data. The other tables in
 that repository (hydzd-variants.txt, twedu-variants.txt, ...) are not
 included. See src/data/character_info/README.md.

Files: src/data/kage/kage_glyphs.tsv
       src/data/kage/kage_layout.tsv
       src/data/kage/kage_subtrees.tsv
       src/data/kage/LICENSE.GlyphWiki
Copyright: 2009, GlyphWiki Project and contributors
License: GlyphWiki-Free-Data
Comment:
 KAGE stroke data and layout tables derived from the GlyphWiki dump. These
 files are plain data read at run time; they are not linked into any binary.
 See src/data/kage/README.kage.md.

Files: vendor/*
Copyright: various upstream authors of Bazel modules and http_archives;
           notably (code built into the binaries): 2000-2003, Nara Institute of Science and Technology
           Okinawa dictionary contributors
           2010-2021, Google Inc.
           2008, Google Inc. (Protocol Buffers)
           Google Inc. (Abseil)
           2008-2019, Susumu Yata (darts-clone, marisa-trie)
           2011, Hiroyuki Komatsu, Shoji Ogura, Tsuyoshi Horo
           2015, THL A29 Limited, a Tencent company, and Milo Yip
           2013-2023, Frank Denis
           1995-2022, Jean-loup Gailly and Mark Adler
           2010-2024, Carbo Kuo and OpenCC contributors
           Unicode, Inc. (CLDR emoji names and annotations)
           Japan Post Co., Ltd. (postal code data; no copyright asserted)
           2024-2026, Marina Pandolfino and Daniel Patrick Morgan
License: Apache-2.0 and BSD-3-Clause and BSD-2-Clause and MIT and ISC and Zlib and Unicode-3.0 and CC0-1.0 and Public-Domain
Comment:
 The vendor/ tree is the Bazel vendor-mode snapshot for offline builds
 (#53). It mixes many upstream projects, each under its own licence
 (abseil Apache-2.0, rules_* Apache-2.0, libsodium ISC, ...). The "and"
 list above names the licences present; it is NOT a per-file audit and
 not every file carries every licence. A per-directory inventory is
 still required before NEW, and pre-built toolchain binaries inside
 vendor/ must go (see DFSG.md, "Known archive blockers").
 .
 Stanzas below with a more specific Files pattern override this one
 (DEP-5: the last matching paragraph wins).

